1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the Stillnote source code, executable software, documentation,
and assets made available under this license, including copies, modifications,
and works derived from them. Separately licensed third-party material is excluded
and remains subject to its own license.

"Licensor" means each copyright holder offering their material under this
license. Each Licensor grants rights only to material they have authority to
license. "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising these rights.

"Internal Use" means use for your own personal activities or your organization's
internal operations, including commercial operations. Employees and contractors
may use the Software on your behalf solely for those operations. Recording,
transcribing, summarizing, and discussing meetings with customers, clients, or
other external participants is Internal Use, provided you do not offer access to
the Software or its functionality as an external product or service.

"Commercial Offering" means a product or service offered to third parties for
payment or other commercial consideration, including a subscription, paid tier,
paid bundle, or a feature used to sell or support another paid product or service.
This includes indirect payment through another product, service, or contract.
Merely using the Software as an internal productivity tool in a paid business,
or sharing the resulting meeting records, is not a Commercial Offering of the
Software.

